PROPOSED USE:
None at this time
RECOMMENDED USE PER ADOPTED LAND USE PLAN:
Public and Quasi-Public
and Parks and Open Space (PlanCheyenne 2006).  The Public and Quasi-Public category includes
existing uses related to community services, such as fire stations, schools, libraries, community
centers, hospitals, civic buildings, utilities and cemeteries. It also includes churches and places of
worship. The Parks and Open Space category includes public and private open space, public and
private parks, country clubs, and golf courses as appropriate uses. Some public utilities or facilities
may also be appropriate. This category may also include natural/cultural resource areas.
DESCRIPTION OF SITE AND SURROUNDINGS:
The site is vacant except for two
accessory buildings utilized by the City Parks Department and several soccer fields. The subdivision
includes portions of Storey Boulevard, Blue Bluff and Canyon Road. Running parallel to Storey
Boulevard is a greenway with a pedestrian underpass under Storey Boulevard west of Canyon Road.
Unincorporated, unplatted state property abuts the subject property to the north. On the east side is
the unincorporated Crestmoor West Subdivision, platted in 1974. On the west side is Mustang Ridge
Subdivision, platted in 1993 and annexed to the City in 1995. On the south side across Storey
Boulevard is Crest Ridge, which was annexed in 1979 and platted the same year in the City.

