### Page 5 of 6

```text
Page 5, Final Plat-12-00005/NCCP-F

Looking east from Chief Washakie along Storey
HISTORY OF AREA:
A portion of the property was annexed in 1987 and the remainder was
annexed with the original plat for North Cheyenne Community Park in 1997. Storey Boulevard
extension was opened in the fall of 2005 in its current location rather than where it was originally
platted.
In 2008, the preliminary plat for the replat was acknowledged and the final plat was submitted on
June 25, 2008, but withdrawn following opposition from neighboring property owners. At that time,
a zone change was being considered concurrently with the platting, which was also withdrawn.
The property is zoned P – Public. The privately owned 4.27-acre Lot 3 is required to be rezoned prior
to any development occurring, in accordance with Section 17.80.010 of the City Code. The current
application is only in regards to the replat.
FINAL PLAT DATA:
This 173.48-acre replat consists of three lots and approximately 11
acres of right-of-way for Storey Boulevard, Blue Bluff, and Canyon Road. The right-of-way for
Storey will be realigned where the road exists and will be wider than the current right-of-way of 100
feet in order to accommodate the existing road and greenway. Canyon and Blue Bluff will remain 60
feet.
Lot 1 is a 40.63-acre school district property. Lot 2 is a 117.52-acre property owned by the City and
containing the North Cheyenne Community Park. Lot 3 is 4.27 acres and is owned by Cheyenne Ice
and Events Center, LP.
If necessary, a development agreement regarding the drainage will be brought before the City
Council for approval prior to recording the plat.
```

### Page 6 of 6

```text
Page 6, Final Plat-12-00005/NCCP-F
REVIEWING AGENCY AND REVIEWERS COMMENTS:
Traffic Engineering:
A Transportation Worksheet to determine TIA/TIS requirements has not been submitted.  A Traffic
Study will be required at such time that the adjacent properties develop (ref. Ch. 3, RSSPDS).
Drainage Engineering:
The proposed Lot 3 is a stormwater detention pond.  This pond was mandated by the City in the early
to mid 1980's for the Crest Ridge development.  The pond was expanded by WyDOT with the Storey
Boulevard project.  There is significant drainage to the pond, and during a 100-year storm more than
80 percent of the lot would be under water.  This lot should be identified on the Plat as a stormwater
pond and/or easements covering the flooded area included with the Plat.  If Lot 3 is proposed to be
developed as anything other than a stormwater pond, at a minimum the existing storage needs to be
replaced prior to development of Lot 3. [Please see the attached drawing of potential drainage
easements.]
Land Record Technician:
Looks generally acceptable.
AGENCIES AND REVIEWERS RESPONDING WITHOUT COMMENTS:
